A||||4||andrewbreen||Gullwing Doors||||5||
Z||000000||andrewbreen||08-20-2000||03:03 PM||||After flipping through a Kit Car magazine with a friend, he commented of how cool the gullwing doors looked on the Lambo and other exotic kits. He then asked me if anyone ever put gullwing's on non-kitted Fiero's, which I had no idea. This got me curious too, because it would add the exotic effect which completely changing the car. Is putting gullwings on a non-kit Fiero possible? Has anyone ever done this? Any input would be appriecated!||||reg||5
Z||000001||JohnnyK||08-20-2000||03:12 PM||||Lamborghini's have scissor-type doors, not gullwing. The DeLorean (man, what a car) and Bricklin had gullwings. It seems to me it would be fairly impossible to mount gullwings on a Fiero, as there is no frame at the top of the door, just window. As for scissor, I have no idea. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||andrewbreen||08-20-2000||05:08 PM||||opps, my bad! I meant the scissor doors, not gullwing. Thanks for clearing that up||||reg||12
Z||000003||Monkeyman||08-21-2000||01:49 AM||||Anything's possible with the right amount of expertise and cash.  You would have to modify most of the side of the car, though.  Door, frame, etc, etc.  If you plan on doing this, I hope you're independently wealthy, 'cause you're gonna go through alot of cash.  It would actually be easier to do a gullwing, but that would be an expensive prospect, too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Taijiguy||08-22-2000||09:58 AM||||I made a suggestion before on the gullwing door, in order to overcome the lack of an upper door frame, design a set of hinges that mount to the sides of the doors, and operate similar to hood hinges; in an out and up manner. It would be relatively easy. (Notice I said RELATIVELY)<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
